{
  "sutta_id": "SN4.8",
  "verses": [
    {
      "number": 1,
      "pali": "Linked Discourses 4.8",
      "english": "Linked Discourses 4.8"
    },
    {
      "number": 2,
      "pali": "Nandana Sutta",
      "english": "Delight"
    },
    {
      "number": 3,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "In this discourse, Māra and Buddha are speaking different languages. By “acquisitions” Māra means one’s family and physical possessions. The Buddha uses the same word to mean a sense of possession for anything—physical or mental—at all."
    },
    {
      "number": 4,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "I have heard that on one occasion the Blessed One was staying near Sāvatthī in Jeta’s Grove, Anāthapiṇḍika’s monastery. Then Māra the Evil One went to the Blessed One and recited this verse in his presence:"
    },
    {
      "number": 5,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“Those with children"
    },
    {
      "number": 6,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "delight"
    },
    {
      "number": 7,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "because of their children."
    },
    {
      "number": 8,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Those with cattle"
    },
    {
      "number": 9,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "delight"
    },
    {
      "number": 10,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "because of their cows."
    },
    {
      "number": 11,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "A person’s delight"
    },
    {
      "number": 12,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "comes from acquisitions,"
    },
    {
      "number": 13,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "since a person with no acquisitions"
    },
    {
      "number": 14,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "doesn’t delight.”"
    },
    {
      "number": 15,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "The Buddha:"
    },
    {
      "number": 16,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "“Those with children"
    },
    {
      "number": 17,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "grieve"
    },
    {
      "number": 18,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "because of their children."
    },
    {
      "number": 19,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Those with cattle"
    },
    {
      "number": 20,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "grieve"
    },
    {
      "number": 21,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "because of their cows."
    },
    {
      "number": 22,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "A person’s grief"
    },
    {
      "number": 23,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "comes from acquisitions,"
    },
    {
      "number": 24,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "since a person with no acquisitions"
    },
    {
      "number": 25,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "doesn’t grieve.”"
    },
    {
      "number": 26,
      "pali": "",
      "english": "Then Māra the Evil One—sad & dejected at realizing, “The Blessed One knows me; the One Well-Gone knows me”—vanished right there."
    }
  ]
}